{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition","id":1489819,"title":"Any ideas for a potential 5th Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-11T17:33:56-07:00","id":1489819,"title":"Any ideas for a potential 5th Edition?","content":"Been thinking about this for a while now. With Vampire and Hunter 5th out, and Werewolf and Mage 5th both being worked on, I've gotten curious about what the other splats would look like in a modern 5th Edition.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any potential speculation on what a 5th Edition of Wraith might end up looking like? I admit, I'm not too familiar with the splat myself; closest thing I came to really playing it was that Afterlife VR game that got released a while back, and even then, it didn't really explain too much of the lore. As a result, I have no idea what a modern version of Wraith would really look like; the only idea I have is a possible rebellion against the Hierarchy, most likely via the Renegades. Anyone have their own opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T21:54:53-07:00","id":1489836,"title":"","content":"If the Fifth Great Maelstrom happened, then Wraith 5 would have no Hierarchy to rebel against; the Dark Kingdoms would all be shattered, and the setting would either be apocalyptic or post-apocalyptic recovery, with a new Wraith society emerging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T08:28:57-07:00","id":1489885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1489836#post1489836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Fifth Great Maelstrom happened, then Wraith 5 would have no Hierarchy to rebel against; the Dark Kingdoms would all be shattered, and the setting would either be apocalyptic or post-apocalyptic recovery, with a new Wraith society emerging.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably meant the Sixth <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Great Maelstrom<br /> <br /> I think maybe the Hierarchy and Dark Kingdoms are still around, but in shambles. Maybe trying to reconstruct. <br /> <br /> I always imagined the setting more like the final scenes from the first Insidious anyway. Maybe Ferrymen lanterns are scattered around kinda like Bloodborne and are the only truly safe place amid the chaos of a constant maelstrom. Make the setting more dangerous and uncertain.<br /> <br /> There is a lot you could do with Wraith if someone really wants to.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:56:04-07:00","id":1490142,"title":"","content":"There have been hints that the Sixth Great Maelstrom may not have happened, instead just being a widespread Level 4 or 5 Maelstrom instead. In this case, expect a mostly status quo. The Hierarchy may be weakened by a resurgent Renegade/Guild/Heretic base. Meaning, a slightly more dynamic metaplot compared to Revises/20th. With the attention to worldwide organizations in the the other Fifth editions, the other Dark Kingdoms may or may not be present. Possibly destroyed or inaccessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T05:21:15-07:00","id":1490247,"title":"","content":"I don't know why Wraith would need a major setting change in order to have a 5th edition, other than that's what Paradox seems to like. <br /> <br /> If we are going that route though:<br /> <br /> Ends of Empire leaves a completely different set of wraiths in charge of Stygia to remake it as they see fit. It would be quite reasonable to run with that into just about anything. I would guess a less restrictive Dictum Mortuum and a more active Stygia, and a battle against the 6th Great Maelstrom and Co, but the nihil-ridden sky is the limit.<br /> <br /> The Wraith Project explored a world where Stygia was gone, the Necropoli were isolated, and Wraiths had to defend against the stormfronts of the 6th Great Maelstrom. It was a fun exploration, as I recall, though I'd prefer a setting that doesn't sideline the Tempest and the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> Then there is Orpheus, which tackled a world where everything was scoured by the 6th Great Maelstrom and the underworld was metaphysically altered by it. Strip out the stuff about living projectors and Grandmother and you have a reasonable setting for NuWraith. I'd really prefer things don't go that way, though. I love Orpheus, but it isn't Wraith and it would not be a good replacement for it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T06:20:55-07:00","id":1490253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1490247#post1490247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why Wraith would need a major setting change in order to have a 5th edition, other than that's what Paradox seems to like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree for the most part. But I don't think anybody here has said that it <i>needs </i>it. We're just <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">speculating on what a 5th Edition of Wraith might end up looking like under Paradox.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T05:35:15-07:00","id":1490375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1490247#post1490247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wraith Project explored a world where Stygia was gone, the Necropoli were isolated, and Wraiths had to defend against the stormfronts of the 6th Great Maelstrom. It was a fun exploration, as I recall, though I'd prefer a setting that doesn't sideline the Tempest and the Labyrinth</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that something official or a fan project? Sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> A splintered Dark Kingdom of Iron with small states and some hegemonies (Holy Roman Empire style) is pretty close to what I imagine as a progressed setting, although I would prefer a somewhat settled 6th Great Maelstrom. Maybe with a re-emergence of the Guilds as a political power and a divide of the military branches of the Legions into mercs and loyalists. I haven't kept up with what happened with Orpheus, but to my understanding it was its own thing?<br /> <br /> The big change on the metaphysical level I would like to see is an increased overlap between the Middle Umbra and the Low Umbra, as a consequence of the 6th GM. I feel introducing Spirits into the setting (still ephemeral, non-plasmic) could be something to freshen it up and fix some mechanical plot-holes, although I realize this is probably a bit controversial.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:26:27-07:00","id":1490391,"title":"","content":"It was a fan project, and it looks like it is mostly gone. Some of the files are still available at <a href=\"https://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/</a>.<br /> <br /> Orpheus was very much its own thing. It is a WoD game and it does follow the Ends of Empire, but it has its own themes and they color much of the game design.<br /> <br /> In Orpheus the 6th Great Maelstrom changed everything, to the point that the game is barely recognizable metaphysically. It actually takes several books before it becomes clear that this is the same world as Wraith. The 6GM wiped out everything. Stygia, the Necropoli, everything. The majority of the game takes place in the skinlands/shadowlands and it is nigh impossible to get further into the Underworld because of the impenatrable Stormwall. When we do finally see it, it is not a stormtossed sea but stormblasted wastelands. Everything was stripped clean. Meanwhile ghosts themselves are manifesting differently, it is (comparatively) easier to Transcend, Drones can be uplifted, Spectres behave oddly, and there's a new threat rising from depths of the void...<br /> <br /> Of course all of these changes were possible because Orpheus was playing by its own themes. None of it really works in Wraith, which is why the Orpheus section in Wr20 was so pared down. <br /> <br /> That would be my issue with mixing the Middle and Low Umbra. I don't think it's controversial so much as it doesn't do much for the themes of Wraith. Most spirits are just general threats and they don't underscore or put pressure on the Wraithly condition, and some even take the pressure off by providing easier access to resources. <br /> <br /> What holes are you trying to fix?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T08:12:48-07:00","id":1490397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1490391#post1490391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a fan project, and it looks like it is mostly gone. Some of the files are still available at <a href=\"https://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/</a>.<br /> <br /> Orpheus was very much its own thing. It is a WoD game and it does follow the Ends of Empire, but it has its own themes and they color much of the game design.<br /> <br /> In Orpheus the 6th Great Maelstrom changed everything, to the point that the game is barely recognizable metaphysically. It actually takes several books before it becomes clear that this is the same world as Wraith. The 6GM wiped out everything. Stygia, the Necropoli, everything. The majority of the game takes place in the skinlands/shadowlands and it is nigh impossible to get further into the Underworld because of the impenatrable Stormwall. When we do finally see it, it is not a stormtossed sea but stormblasted wastelands. Everything was stripped clean. Meanwhile ghosts themselves are manifesting differently, it is (comparatively) easier to Transcend, Drones can be uplifted, Spectres behave oddly, and there's a new threat rising from depths of the void...<br /> <br /> Of course all of these changes were possible because Orpheus was playing by its own themes. None of it really works in Wraith, which is why the Orpheus section in Wr20 was so pared down.<br /> <br /> That would be my issue with mixing the Middle and Low Umbra. I don't think it's controversial so much as it doesn't do much for the themes of Wraith. Most spirits are just general threats and they don't underscore or put pressure on the Wraithly condition, and some even take the pressure off by providing easier access to resources.<br /> <br /> What holes are you trying to fix?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the info!<br /> <br /> As for the Spirit thing, there are several issues, but the main point for me would be a buffer between Wraiths and Skinland interaction that is a bit more sturdy than the Dictum Mortuum and the Shroud. I've used them (admittedly, in just the single campaign I ran) as a tool to have natural wards on things I didn't want the players to mess with that were outside the scope of the factions the setting provided. As an exaggerated example, what is stopping a Spectre with Inhabit from walking into an NPP and mess with the cooling rods?<br /> <br /> Mind, I still want the two Umbrae separated, and the interaction limited. But I like the idea of ephemeral entities in the Shadowlands that could provide more ambience. Make a new type of Spirit called Memories that project as spectral forests or a murder of ghostly (no pun intended) ravens. That seems more functional to me than using plasmics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T07:14:10-07:00","id":1490511,"title":"","content":"I can see where you are coming from. For my part, I don't think the goal is to impede Wraiths from interacting with the living, I think it is to make it risky. If the Dictum Mortuum disappeared I would see the need for something else to drive that risk, and predatory emotion spirits attracted to human fear could work. Outside of that, I wouldn't do much to increase the difficulty of interacting with the living.<br /> <br /> As for Spectres and power plants, they have a significantly harder time interacting with the living world or even seeing the living. Very few Spectres will have the right combination of mindset, powers, and capabilities to plan and successfully carry out an attack on the living of that magnitude. Few enough that it's not cheating to just leave them out of the game. Going after targets important to the PCs is another matter.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of the ambiance of a deeper emotional ecology to the Shadowlands, though I'd have them originate in the Low Umbra. Memories and emotion are the stuff of the Underworld after all. My main consideration is that they can't be an easy replacement for soulsteel or relics. That's easy to handwave, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T10:09:12-07:00","id":1490518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1490511#post1490511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see where you are coming from. For my part, I don't think the goal is to impede Wraiths from interacting with the living, I think it is to make it risky. If the Dictum Mortuum disappeared I would see the need for something else to drive that risk, and predatory emotion spirits attracted to human fear could work. Outside of that, I wouldn't do much to increase the difficulty of interacting with the living.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, exactly. My example was very strict, but I picture them more like a neutral party that <i>can</i> be territorial, very similar to how they work in WtA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1490511#post1490511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Spectres and power plants, they have a significantly harder time interacting with the living world or even seeing the living. Very few Spectres will have the right combination of mindset, powers, and capabilities to plan and successfully carry out an attack on the living of that magnitude. Few enough that it's not cheating to just leave them out of the game. Going after targets important to the PCs is another matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe picking a Spectre was a mistake; I meant to illustrate a problem where there is very sensitive Skinland infrastructure (not just NPPs) that is very vulnerable to Wraiths, and in most cases would not be 'protected' by any party that can actually do something about it. Because I was used to powerful places like that having Spirits that can defend their Domains from running WtA games, I defaulted to them. But as far as I know, there is no interaction mechanic between Middle Umbra Spirits and Wraiths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1490511#post1490511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the idea of the ambiance of a deeper emotional ecology to the Shadowlands, though I'd have them originate in the Low Umbra. Memories and emotion are the stuff of the Underworld after all. My main consideration is that they can't be an easy replacement for soulsteel or relics. That's easy to handwave, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no corpus, no soulsteel. I could see some kind of Pathos exchange mechanic, though. In general, an additional population outside Necropolises and points of interaction if needed wouldn't be a bad thing; as it is, the Shadowlands can be pretty empty. I haven't completely thought it through, but my gut says there is some good metaphysical potential to give the Spirits an important role in the mechanics of the Underworld as a link to the Skinlands- especially if it is a native kind, as you said. And sometimes, having the option of having the shade of a cat run around a street corner is just nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-17-2022, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T11:59:27-07:00","id":1494744,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd be happy for Wraith to stay as it is -- in the forever-maybe-never-land of Wr20. It seems kinda poetic not to rouse the Beast for something that might ruin what it was.<br /> <br /> That said, I see Wraith: The Great War as a good model for how wraith society might survive the Sixth Great Maelstrom, but amp it up even more. Make Stygia a great unknown your characters can seek out or ignore as they wish. Everything would be more isolated, but not necessarily completely destroyed.<br /> <br /> Using V5 as an example, which uses parts of the Gehenna plot but not all of it, it might just be that the Sixth Great Maelstrom is neverending but doesn't completely obliterate Stygia. It would do for the setting what the Avatar Storm did for Mage, without completing nuking the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T05:49:45-07:00","id":1494965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1494744#post1494744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd be happy for Wraith to stay as it is -- in the forever-maybe-never-land of Wr20. It seems kinda poetic not to rouse the Beast for something that might ruin what it was.<br /> <br /> That said, I see Wraith: The Great War as a good model for how wraith society might survive the Sixth Great Maelstrom, but amp it up even more. Make Stygia a great unknown your characters can seek out or ignore as they wish. Everything would be more isolated, but not necessarily completely destroyed.<br /> <br /> Using V5 as an example, which uses parts of the Gehenna plot but not all of it, it might just be that the Sixth Great Maelstrom is neverending but doesn't completely obliterate Stygia. It would do for the setting what the Avatar Storm did for Mage, without completing nuking the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if W5 ends up being an actual continuation of W20? Anything you'd like to see? Any ideas for stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T08:20:25-07:00","id":1495072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1494965#post1494965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if W5 ends up being an actual continuation of W20? Anything you'd like to see? Any ideas for stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>The chance that nWW will do that after breaking from old material on three prior lines is practically zero squared.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T19:49:56-07:00","id":1495297,"title":"","content":"I would probably abandon the separate Shadowguide thing. It's just too unwieldy if you have more than two players. With the Hunger and Desperation mechanics, I think there's a foundation for a kind of player initiated (or at least player regulated) risk/reward system that could replace it. <br /> <br /> In the spirit of the back-to-basics V5/H5, you'd probably want to de-center Stygia and instead focus on local communities of ghosts haunting the real world, rather than the weird gothic fantasy kingdom that is Stygia. And I say that as someone who likes weird gothic fantasy kingdoms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T13:17:40-08:00","id":1501048,"title":"","content":"The 5th editions follow the Orpheus stotyline. Not only Orpheus appears in Hunter 5th edition, but also there are some wraiths as antagonists and in the background of one of them is mentioned the devastation of the &quot;imperial burocracy&quot; that had him slaved. In the Vampire 5th edition books there are also hints about End of the empire having happened, for example, the Orphans of Enoch faction in Forbidden religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 01-22-2023, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:45:50-08:00","id":1501499,"title":"","content":"Lets be honest, a Sixth Maelstrom happening out of the blue without any significant event in the REAL world is just kinda of silly.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, Covid and war in Ukraine seem significant, but if we were to look at history, they really arent. We just think they are because we are living them at the moment, but both truly are minimal.<br /> <br /> As of right now, a 6th Maelstrom capable of wrecking the Underworld could only ever be justified or justifiable if we go over a nuclear apocalypse.<br /> <br /> But in that case, we wouldn't need to worry about that for the game, since we would either be very very dead or trying to survive in an unforgiving world of a nuclear winter, so... I hope they dont bring some 6th Maelstrom garbage into the game. Not until the end of OUR world, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T14:34:08-08:00","id":1501744,"title":"","content":"That is just an opinion, based on a questionable reasoning and could be applied to every other maelstrom, actually. For example, the first maelstrom was just the falling of one of the many empires that the ancient world had. How many times fell China, Babylon or Egypt without maelstrom involved? In the end, the maelstrom are not logic, coherent or anything else, they are a plot device. And if the authors want to state that the 6th maelstrom happened or is happening (as the Gehenna in Vampire) is just a narrative choice not connected necessarily to any real world event. In fact, when they wrote it, it was the death of supernatural being what triggered it. I understand the reluctance to chance and to accept that a new edition could shake drastically the setting we love, but it is going to change, drastically, everything points to the Hierarchy having fall and Orpheus doing businesses. We can keep playing Wr20 forever anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T16:26:30-08:00","id":1501756,"title":"","content":"How about this: the Dark Kingdom of Iron <i>did </i>fall, and Orpheus <i>did </i>gain a foothold in the Underworld. But that was almost 25 years ago; and unlike the Orpheus gameline, the 6th Great Maelstrom didn't scour the Underworld clean. Likewise, unlike the first edition of HtR, ghosts weren't forced across the Shroud and into the Skinlands <i>en mass</i>. Since then, the Great Maelstrom has subsided and a new Hierarchy has begun to rise. It isn't yet to the same level of power as the old Hierarchy had achieved before its demise; and with Orpheus in the mix now, it has more challenges to overcome than its precessor had. <br /> <br /> Where the Hierarchy holds sway, you can run the same sorts of games as you can with Wraith 20, with one difference: the Guilds are back, as a foundational part of the new Hierarchy. But there are also many more Necropoli than there used to be that <i>aren't </i>part of the new Dark Kingdom of Iron. There are now whole Necropoli that are run by what earlier editions would have called Renegades. They're now independent city-states; if the Storyteller chooses to use one of them as the focus of his chronicle, the result will be somewhat similar to the Wraith Project mentioned earlier in this thread: the Necropolis will basically be on its own against the threats faced in the Shadowlands. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> The new Hierarchy has to contend with more threats than its precessor did: it <i>used to be</i> that the only thing you had to worry about was Spectres from the Tempest; but now there's a renewed danger from the Skinlands as well: with Orpheus and its rivals in play, the exploitation of the dead by the living is in full force. The new version of the Dictum Mortuum isn't so much a command as it is good advice: wraiths who interact with the living are <i>far</i> more likely these days to run afoul of ghost hunters. If you want to run a chronicle that deals more heavily with the Skinlands, one option is to partake in the Hierarchy's war against Orpheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T01:55:59-08:00","id":1501789,"title":"","content":"Before enumerating them, my elucubrations are based on the supposition that the authors will want to bring back the focus to &quot;ghost stories&quot;, instead of the dark fantasy of the Underworld. So I think they are going to:<br /> <br /> 1 Follow the Orpheus plot of the Underworld being wiped out. Stygia fallen, the Dark Kingdom of Jade fallen, everything else lost contact. The hierarchy, guilds and structures of the Underworld completely destroyed. Some Necropolis could have survived, and there the Hierarchy could have evolved to something else more local and isolated, feudal kingdoms of the anacreons, but not empires.<br /> <br /> 2 Put the focus on pathos, shadows and fetters. I think the focus of the next edition is going to shift towards a more personal horror, without the political machinations of the hierarchy, the wars between empires or the labyrinth as a place you could visit. Spectres would keep existing, but as something more vague and alien, completely unknown and unplayable (the castes blurred).<br /> <br /> 3 Strengthen the tempest, which means the game would have place between the skinlands and the shadowlands. Beyond, the 6th maelstrom still rages on. That contributes to the former points.<br /> <br /> 4 Orpheus could an antagonistic or a player option, they are a corporation exploring the underworld after all. And Terrel &amp; Squib would be definitively antagonistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 01-31-2023, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T02:34:01-08:00","id":1501791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1501789#post1501789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before enumerating them, my elucubrations are based on the supposition that the authors will want to bring back the focus to &quot;ghost stories&quot;, instead of the dark fantasy of the Underworld. So I think they are going to:<br /> <br /> 1 Follow the Orpheus plot of the Underworld being wiped out. Stygia fallen, the Dark Kingdom of Jade fallen, everything else lost contact. The hierarchy, guilds and structures of the Underworld completely destroyed. Some Necropolis could have survived, and there the Hierarchy could have evolved to something else more local and isolated, feudal kingdoms of the anacreons, but not empires.<br /> <br /> 2 Put the focus on pathos, shadows and fetters. I think the focus of the next edition is going to shift towards a more personal horror, without the political machinations of the hierarchy, the wars between empires or the labyrinth as a place you could visit. Spectres would keep existing, but as something more vague and alien, completely unknown and unplayable (the castes blurred).<br /> <br /> 3 Strengthen the tempest, which means the game would have place between the skinlands and the shadowlands. Beyond, the 6th maelstrom still rages on. That contributes to the former points.<br /> <br /> 4 Orpheus could an antagonistic or a player option, they are a corporation exploring the underworld after all. And Terrel &amp; Squib would be definitively antagonistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I basically drafted a really long post covering a lot of the same ground, then my phone's &quot;digital wellbeing tools&quot; kicked me out of Brave for being online too long, and the website didn't save my text. Damn it!<br /> <br /> But as you've ninja'd me now, I'll just say I agree with these ideas. I will say why I think WTO focused on all the dark urban fantasy stuff, though.<br /> <br /> As you suggest, there were always (at least) two broad playstyles for <i>Wraith</i>: one was the ghost stories thing, and the other was the dark urban fantasy sandbox, which is also what VTM and CTD often defaulted to.<br /> <br /> I think even the 1e core book writers knew that while WTO had a really appealing world and core concept, it didn't create a lot of active drama for players if played the way it was intended.<br /> <br /> You could sort of narrate how you were moping around, looking at your mortal life as it fades away, protecting your Fetters and trying to resolve your Passions, but that was all very emotionally intensive, required a lot of interiority that doesn't work in a TTRPG (as opposed to in a novel, say) and gets repetitive quickly. It's hard work and not necessarily always fun. It creates a huge barrier for entry, too.<br /> <br /> The writers knew that on some level, so they created this byzantine bureaucracy to interact with and a really detailed Underworld for you to explore. And this part of the game rapidly expanded as the gameline did, because it was far more playable.<br /> <br /> The first supplement, for example, was <i>Necropolis: Atlanta</i>, and that immediately set the stage for what this dark urban fantasy sandbox would look like. It's the basic pattern established by VTM and <i>Chicago by Night</i>.<br /> <br /> We had a few books like <i>Love Beyond Death</i>, but that actually came out after we'd already had books like <i>The Midnight Express</i>, which was pulling players towards Stygia and the Tempest. And honestly, I don't think the WoD would've ever been as popular as it was without those kitchen sink settings that could draw in a diverse range of players.<br /> <br /> Within a year of WTO landing, you could adventure in the Dark Kingdom of Jade and explore the Sea of Shadows. With books like <i>Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth</i>, you could even play <i>Aliens</i> via <i>Beetlejuice</i>.<br /> <br /> Wr5 will probably jettison most of that, as you say. They probably will keep <i>some</i> of the dark urban fantasy sandboxy stuff, because they know that's a big draw for <i>Vampire</i>, but it will be lessened so that it doesn't become the main game.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Hierarchy will probably be fractured, and functioning like independent colonies rather than a huge, Underworld-spanning empire. More like the Camarilla of V5 than the Camarilla of 1e to V20.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Hierarchs will have all retreated to their Citadels, leaving the rest of the Necropoli to the others. Between cities will just be an endless storm, so there won't be much communication between Necropoli.<br /> <br /> Renegades will be more powerful, Heretics will be on the prowl for new recruits, and travel into the Tempest and to Stygia will be very difficult indeed. There may be no central ruler of the Hierarchy, unless there's a group of new Deathlords, but they might make it fuzzy enough that the DLs have just retreated rather than definitely been destroyed. Charon will be gone.<br /> <br /> I think it is do-able, but the risk will be that it's more H5 than V5, and so there might not be a lot to do besides the one &quot;focus&quot; that the devs decide on. And for <i>Wraith</i>, that may be enough to guarantee its death (again). Because it was always a hard sell, and that &quot;personal horror&quot; version of the game was the hardest part of the setting.<br /> <br /> <i>Orpheus</i> strikes me as more likely to get the 5th Edition treatment than WTO, as it has a clearer focus and nukes the metaplot. It's much more newbie friendly, as well, which is a big focus for WW/Paradox now.<br /> <br /> But <i>Orpheus</i> is not entirely consistent with the way wraiths work in WTO (e.g., Shadows are more like Pasiphae in Orpheus, which could fit into WTO, but may require some in-character justification for why Shadows are independent beings now). And there may not be much scope to play wraiths in that game at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 02-01-2023, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T03:08:17-08:00","id":1501793,"title":"","content":"I've got a couple of (largely negative and very bitter) predictions.<br /> Angst dice are rather obvious. I foresee the shadowguide component getting jettisoned and the shadow becoming more like the beast of the vampire (possibly shadow natures will be like clan compulsions). I don't know whether they'll rename fetters to touchstones to keep them in theme with the other gamelines, or use the terms as synonyms or what.<br /> <br /> I'd also concur with the idea that the Dark Kingdoms will be reduced, assuming they still exist and weren't wiped out in a maelstrom. If WoD5 follows the same pattern its currently on* it's going to be &quot;street level&quot; (gameplay only occurs in the Shadowlands moping around after touchstones/fetters, no adventures in the rest of the underworld because apparently that detracts from personal horror stories or whatever). Possibly everything all the way down to the Labyrinth will be &quot;too dangerous&quot; to access, like the Umbra in Werewolf-5. Also because WoD is Punk, you must be Punks fighting against The Man. If the Hierarchy still exists then you will play as a member of a circle of Renegades, if not then The Man is Orpheus.**<br /> At least one of the legions and/or guilds will be totally altered for reasons that completely miss the point.<br /> <br /> *Assuming of course that it does, because they've changed creative direction <i>again </i>so who knows where they're headed next.<br /> **Assuming that they don't pull a Hunter&quot;5&quot; and it turns out that it's actually a new edition of Orpheus under the name Wraith: the Oblivion, possibly with bits of Geist slapped on regardless of whether they make sense or not.\u200b<br /> <br /> All this, of course, assumes that there's going to be a WtO5, as opposed to just making a new setting with enough of the elements of WtO to get away with using the name. Werewolf is one of the main three gamelines and got that treatment, Wraith would probably get lumped in Hunter, being considered as not having a significant enough fanbase to matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: It just occured to me that possibly the Dark Kingdoms could get the Sabbat/Get treatment, the maelstrom consumes everything within the tempest and everything within it falls to Oblivion becoming warped, Labyrinth-like citadels populated with armies of spectres. I don't want it, but that does sound cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 01-31-2023, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T03:33:47-08:00","id":1501795,"title":"","content":"That is exactly my reasoning about how the game evolved and will evolve, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T07:06:09-08:00","id":1501810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1501793#post1501793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: It just occured to me that possibly the Dark Kingdoms could get the Sabbat/Get treatment, the maelstrom consumes everything within the tempest and everything within it falls to Oblivion becoming warped, Labyrinth-like citadels populated with armies of spectres. I don't want it, but that does sound cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was basically what <b>Orpheus</b> did: the Shroud became an impassible Stormwall, and everything in the other side got consumed by the Tempest. In my more jaded moments, I tend to think that ParaWolf will end up making <b>Wr5</b> as a reskinned <b>Orpheus</b>, jettisoning the plot that <b>Orpheus</b> featured but keeping the idea (from nearly every book after the first one in that series) that you're <i>not</i> working for Orpheus or anyone else.<br /> <br /> That is, they're likely to take the Nature Categories, Shades, Horrors, and Vitality/Spite/Stains and Crucible systems from <b>Orpheus</b>, and <i>possibly </i>even the Laments* while jettisoning the assumption that you are or were connected in any way to Orpheus, downplaying its existence to just another element in the setting. I could <i>especially </i>see the <b>Orpheus</b>-style Shades being given a prominent role in this vision of <b>Wr5</b>, complete with the idea that all playable wraiths have an innate ability to Manifest in the Skinlands. <br /> <br /> <b>Orpheus</b> <i>was</i>, after all, an attempt to reframe the \u201cplay a ghost\u201d gameline in a way that \u201clearned from the mistakes made by <b>Wraith</b>\u201d. And given what they did with <b>Hunter</b>, I wouldn't put it past them to try to do something similarly radical to <b>Wraith</b>. <br /> <br /> And given ParaWolf's propensity to borrow elements from Chronicles of Darkness, I could also see them doing things like incorporating ideas from <b>Geist</b> into this. If they don't go with <b>Orpheus</b>' \u201cSpirits have evil twins\u201d idea, they <i>might</i> try to adapt <b>Geist</b>'s notion of Synergy instead, saying that part of the personal horror of the game is that you need to face your Shadow and come to terms with it. If they do, then the Shades would take on elements of <b>Geist</b>'s Burdens \u2014 though on the positives side, this might allow us to retain something akin to <b>Wraith</b>'s Passions in the form of a reskinning of a Burden's Aspiration. They might also incorporate concepts from <b>Geist</b>'s krewes into <b>Orpheus</b>' Crucibles, making Crucibles the central social organizing principle of the game instead of empires of the dead or corporate masters. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#999999\">* though I could also see them saying that the Spirit Lament is ubiquitous; this would, after all, technically be <b>Wraith</b>, not <b>Geist</b>. And even if they keep the Laments, they might do something like renaming the Spirit Lament as the Wraith Lament, making it the default option, and relegating the others to an Appendix focused on Wraith-adjacent gameplay. Maybe even turn the Risen into a \u201cfifth Lament\u201d.<br /> <br /> I could see them keeping the full range of Laments around, and possibly even expanding on it, because ParaWolf seems to like borrowing ideas from the Chronicles of Darkness when updating their World of Darkness gamelines to X5; and having Projectors and Risen and possibly other \u201cback from the dead and once again among the living\u201d character options would make it easier to incorporate ideas from <b>Geist</b> into <b>Wr5</b>. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T11:18:43-08:00","id":1501891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1501793#post1501793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd also concur with the idea that the Dark Kingdoms will be reduced, assuming they still exist and weren't wiped out in a maelstrom. If WoD5 follows the same pattern its currently on* it's going to be &quot;street level&quot; (gameplay only occurs in the Shadowlands moping around after touchstones/fetters, no adventures in the rest of the underworld because apparently that detracts from personal horror stories or whatever). Possibly everything all the way down to the Labyrinth will be &quot;too dangerous&quot; to access, like the Umbra in Werewolf-5. Also because WoD is Punk, you must be Punks fighting against The Man. If the Hierarchy still exists then you will play as a member of a circle of Renegades, if not then The Man is Orpheus.**<br /> At least one of the legions and/or guilds will be totally altered for reasons that completely miss the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how far the Umbra is reduced in W:tA, one wonders if the cosmology of the new setting will even let Wraith be a thing. I mean, they might have already given the &quot;4th WoD line&quot; slot over to Hunter... as far as one can call H5 &quot;Hunter&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T12:39:53-08:00","id":1501899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1501891#post1501891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how far the Umbra is reduced in W:tA, one wonders if the cosmology of the new setting will even let Wraith be a thing. I mean, they might have already given the &quot;4th WoD line&quot; slot over to Hunter... as far as one can call H5 &quot;Hunter&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of how deliberately butchered the Umbra has been in W:tA, I dread to see how W:tO will be handled...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T22:40:59-07:00","id":1507552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489819-any-ideas-for-a-potential-5th-edition?p=1501791#post1501791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I basically drafted a really long post covering a lot of the same ground, then my phone's &quot;digital wellbeing tools&quot; kicked me out of Brave for being online too long, and the website didn't save my text. Damn it!<br /> <br /> But as you've ninja'd me now, I'll just say I agree with these ideas. I will say why I think WTO focused on all the dark urban fantasy stuff, though.<br /> <br /> As you suggest, there were always (at least) two broad playstyles for <i>Wraith</i>: one was the ghost stories thing, and the other was the dark urban fantasy sandbox, which is also what VTM and CTD often defaulted to.<br /> <br /> I think even the 1e core book writers knew that while WTO had a really appealing world and core concept, it didn't create a lot of active drama for players if played the way it was intended.<br /> <br /> You could sort of narrate how you were moping around, looking at your mortal life as it fades away, protecting your Fetters and trying to resolve your Passions, but that was all very emotionally intensive, required a lot of interiority that doesn't work in a TTRPG (as opposed to in a novel, say) and gets repetitive quickly. It's hard work and not necessarily always fun. It creates a huge barrier for entry, too.<br /> <br /> The writers knew that on some level, so they created this byzantine bureaucracy to interact with and a really detailed Underworld for you to explore. And this part of the game rapidly expanded as the gameline did, because it was far more playable.<br /> <br /> The first supplement, for example, was <i>Necropolis: Atlanta</i>, and that immediately set the stage for what this dark urban fantasy sandbox would look like. It's the basic pattern established by VTM and <i>Chicago by Night</i>.<br /> <br /> We had a few books like <i>Love Beyond Death</i>, but that actually came out after we'd already had books like <i>The Midnight Express</i>, which was pulling players towards Stygia and the Tempest. And honestly, I don't think the WoD would've ever been as popular as it was without those kitchen sink settings that could draw in a diverse range of players.<br /> <br /> Within a year of WTO landing, you could adventure in the Dark Kingdom of Jade and explore the Sea of Shadows. With books like <i>Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth</i>, you could even play <i>Aliens</i> via <i>Beetlejuice</i>.<br /> <br /> Wr5 will probably jettison most of that, as you say. They probably will keep <i>some</i> of the dark urban fantasy sandboxy stuff, because they know that's a big draw for <i>Vampire</i>, but it will be lessened so that it doesn't become the main game.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Hierarchy will probably be fractured, and functioning like independent colonies rather than a huge, Underworld-spanning empire. More like the Camarilla of V5 than the Camarilla of 1e to V20.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Hierarchs will have all retreated to their Citadels, leaving the rest of the Necropoli to the others. Between cities will just be an endless storm, so there won't be much communication between Necropoli.<br /> <br /> Renegades will be more powerful, Heretics will be on the prowl for new recruits, and travel into the Tempest and to Stygia will be very difficult indeed. There may be no central ruler of the Hierarchy, unless there's a group of new Deathlords, but they might make it fuzzy enough that the DLs have just retreated rather than definitely been destroyed. Charon will be gone.<br /> <br /> I think it is do-able, but the risk will be that it's more H5 than V5, and so there might not be a lot to do besides the one &quot;focus&quot; that the devs decide on. And for <i>Wraith</i>, that may be enough to guarantee its death (again). Because it was always a hard sell, and that &quot;personal horror&quot; version of the game was the hardest part of the setting.<br /> <br /> <i>Orpheus</i> strikes me as more likely to get the 5th Edition treatment than WTO, as it has a clearer focus and nukes the metaplot. It's much more newbie friendly, as well, which is a big focus for WW/Paradox now.<br /> <br /> But <i>Orpheus</i> is not entirely consistent with the way wraiths work in WTO (e.g., Shadows are more like Pasiphae in Orpheus, which could fit into WTO, but may require some in-character justification for why Shadows are independent beings now). And there may not be much scope to play wraiths in that game at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of your ideas. In addition to that, &quot;Hello! I'm back from the Mouth of the Void (aka two-year-long depression after my father's death by COVID-19&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}